    "result": "Excellent! All 28 tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n**Issue 1: governance test** - `APPROVAL_STATUSES` was not exported as a named export from `src/finetune/index.js`\n- **Fix**: Added named exports for the schema constants (`APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `DEFAULT_GOVERNANCE_TEMPLATE`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, `RISK_LEVELS`)\n\n**Issue 2: eval test** - `toxicityMetric` was receiving `references` as the second parameter, but only expects `outputs`\n- **Fix**: Modified `runEvaluations` to check each metric's `function.length` property. Functions with `length >= 2` receive both outputs and references, while those with `length < 2` (like `toxicityMetric` with its default parameter) only receive outputs. This respects each metric's actual signature.\n\nBoth fixes maintain backward compatibility and preserve all existing public exports.",
